<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  JawaEyeGlow_Stock.xml                      Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-11
  ============================================================================

  Companion to Defs/GeneDefs/JawaEyeColours.xml. That file gives our two
  authored eye genes a glow texture and a glow shader; this gives the SAME
  treatment to the stock gene BTD_Jawa also carries, so all three roll results
  match instead of one of them staying flat.

      Jawa_Eyes_HugeOrange     MoteGlow              (ours, in the GeneDef)
      Jawa_Eyes_HugeAmber      MoteGlow              (ours, in the GeneDef)
      guy762_Eyes_HugeYellow   MoteGlow              (here)

  ⚠️ ALL THREE ARE MoteGlow, DELIBERATELY. DO NOT RE-SPREAD THEM.

  This file once ran a three-shader comparison — the engine picks one gene per
  pawn and BTD_Jawa lists all three, so one load scored all three side by side.
  That experiment is FINISHED (commit 263e539, 2026-08-11). A night screenshot
  at Dark 0% split the pawns almost exactly along shader lines, 9 glowing to 6
  black:

      MoteGlowPulseLow   renders too dim to see at all on a pawn render node
      MoteGlowPulse      "so subtle I can't really tell" after two loads of it
      MoteGlow           the one that works — steady, and the canon read anyway

  The pulse is gone for a structural reason, not a taste one: a per-pawn phase
  offset and a floored trough need C#, and a shader-driven global sine was never
  going to deliver them. Two unblinking lights under a hood is the target.

  TransparentPostLight remains the documented FALLBACK, not a variant to test.
  It draws after the lighting pass, so the eyes hold full brightness in pitch
  dark without being additive. Reach for it only if MoteGlow reads as a flat
  white blob, and then move all three together.

  ⚠️ THIS EDITS ANOTHER MOD'S GENE. guy762_Eyes_HugeYellow belongs to Star Wars
  Xenotypes and is not Jawa-only, so any other xenotype carrying it also gets
  the glow. Checked against the resolved load set: it appears on BTD_Jawa and
  guy762_xenotype_jawa and nothing else, so the blast radius is Jawa either way.
  If a future update spreads it wider, this becomes a wider change.

  The texture swap is the load-bearing half. The donor art is flat (255,255,0)
  across the whole ellipse, so a <color> tint can only ever produce flat paint.
  jawaeyes_glow.png regrades the interior to a white-hot core with a rim at 62%,
  and because gene tinting MULTIPLIES, the core resolves to the full saturated
  colour and the rim resolves dark. That gradient is what reads as emission.

  ⚠️ 2026-08-12 — THE ALPHA CHANNEL WAS FIXED. The RGB gradient above is
  unchanged; do not re-flatten it.

  Observed in game at 1 AM, zoomed in (Steam screenshot 20260812132104): each
  eye had a visible ring around it. Cause, measured from the PNG rather than
  guessed — the sprite's radial gradient ran all the way out to near-black
  (18,12,4) but stayed at ALPHA 255 the whole way. That outer band was 1,572 px,
  **41% of the entire visible sprite**, and (18,12,4) is fractionally LIGHTER
  and warmer than the Jawa hood's true black, so it drew as a distinct ring
  around the glow rather than disappearing into the hood.

  Fix: alpha now tracks luminance through a knee — fully transparent at or below
  L=14, fully opaque at or above L=45, linear between. RGB untouched, so the
  MULTIPLY tint behaviour described above still holds exactly. Result: 1,572
  opaque dark pixels went to alpha 0, zero remain, and the bright core and the
  faint outer bloom both kept their original alpha.

  The bloom that survives is a ~3 px band on a 168 px canvas drawn at drawSize
  0.16, i.e. sub-pixel on screen — it is the intended soft glow, not a ring.

  ⚠️ GENERAL RULE THIS COST A ZOOM-IN TO LEARN: in a glow sprite, alpha must
  track brightness. Opaque near-black pixels are not invisible — they occlude,
  and they draw a disc wherever the background is darker than they are.

  SAFETY AND LOAD ORDER
  =====================
  Both ops are conditional on the exact node, so they self-disable if Star Wars
  Xenotypes restructures the gene. Star Wars Xenotypes is load 545 and
  Jawa_Patches is 564.

  Two ops rather than one because the gene has a separate render node per eye
  and each needs its own texPath and shader.

  VERIFY AFTER THE NEXT LOAD
  ==========================
    * Spawn ~20 Jawa and compare the three treatments. Pick one; make the other
      two match it.
    * Look at them at night and in an unlit room. That is the whole point.
    * If any reads as a flat white blob, the additive Mote shader is wrong for
      a pawn node; move that gene to TransparentPostLight.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/GeneDef[defName="guy762_Eyes_HugeYellow"]/renderNodeProperties/li[1]/texPath</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/GeneDef[defName="guy762_Eyes_HugeYellow"]/renderNodeProperties/li[1]/texPath</xpath>
          <value>
            <texPath>JawaEyes/jawaeyes_glow</texPath>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/GeneDef[defName="guy762_Eyes_HugeYellow"]/renderNodeProperties/li[1]</xpath>
          <value>
            <shaderTypeDef>MoteGlow</shaderTypeDef>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/GeneDef[defName="guy762_Eyes_HugeYellow"]/renderNodeProperties/li[1]/drawSize</xpath>
          <value>
            <drawSize>0.16</drawSize>
          </value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/GeneDef[defName="guy762_Eyes_HugeYellow"]/renderNodeProperties/li[2]/texPath</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/GeneDef[defName="guy762_Eyes_HugeYellow"]/renderNodeProperties/li[2]/texPath</xpath>
          <value>
            <texPath>JawaEyes/jawaeyes_glow</texPath>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/GeneDef[defName="guy762_Eyes_HugeYellow"]/renderNodeProperties/li[2]</xpath>
          <value>
            <shaderTypeDef>MoteGlow</shaderTypeDef>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/GeneDef[defName="guy762_Eyes_HugeYellow"]/renderNodeProperties/li[2]/drawSize</xpath>
          <value>
            <drawSize>0.16</drawSize>
          </value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
